{"task": "Prove exactly this local conditional obligation using the supplied NL route. Return only the tactic body through submit_transition. All displayed parameter and input proof binders are already in context.", "packet": {"version": 2, "contract_sha256": "3575d5d75c1eb2aaf8b92e3182b02e09afba2fd0f4d1ab9e569e2cc16c872495", "header": "import Mathlib

open scoped ENNReal NNReal BigOperators

abbrev YuiEucl (n : ℕ) := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)
def YuiI : Set ℝ := Set.Icc 0 1
def YuiSnoc {n : ℕ} (x : YuiEucl n) (t : ℝ) : YuiEucl (n + 1) :=
  WithLp.toLp 2 (Fin.snoc (fun i => x i) t)
def YuiHead {n : ℕ} (z : YuiEucl (n + 1)) : YuiEucl n :=
  WithLp.toLp 2 (fun i : Fin n => z i.castSucc)
def YuiLast {n : ℕ} (z : YuiEucl (n + 1)) : ℝ := z (Fin.last n)
def YuiCylinder {n : ℕ} (E : Set (YuiEucl n)) : Set (YuiEucl (n + 1)) :=
  {z | YuiHead z ∈ E ∧ YuiLast z ∈ YuiI}
noncomputable def YuiCost {X : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace X] {ι : Type*}
    (s : ℝ) (U : ι → Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ∑' i, ⨆ (_ : (U i).Nonempty), (Metric.ediam (U i)) ^ s
def YuiCover {X : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace X] (δ : ℝ) (A : Set X)
    (U : ℕ → Set X) : Prop :=
  A ⊆ ⋃ i, U i ∧ ∀ i, Metric.ediam (U i) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal δ
noncomputable def YuiContent {X : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace X]
    (s δ : ℝ) (A : Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ⨅ (U : ℕ → Set X) (_ : YuiCover δ A U), YuiCost s U
noncomputable def YuiMeasure {X : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace X]
    (s : ℝ) (A : Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ⨆ (δ : ℝ) (_ : 0 < δ), YuiContent s δ A
", "parameters": [{"name": "n", "type": "ℕ"}, {"name": "E", "type": "Set (YuiEucl n)"}], "representation": "Use EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)=PiLp 2 (constant ℝ), indexed by Fin n, with its native L2 metric and Borel structure; n is a natural ambient dimension including 0. YuiSnoc appends a real coordinate and YuiHead/YuiLast recover it; YuiCylinder E is defined by these coordinates directly in EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n+1)). T003 checks the coordinate inverse and Euclidean distance identities used by all cylinder arguments, so there is no max-product metric or unproved metric replacement. The interval remains Set.Icc (0:ℝ) 1. Metric.ediam, YuiCost, YuiContent and YuiMeasure take values in ℝ≥0∞; ^ with a real exponent is ENNReal.rpow. The supremum over a nonempty witness equals ediam^s and over an empty witness equals zero, giving the prescribed empty-cover convention even at exponent zero. All uses of Hausdorff content or normalization are guarded by s>0 and δ>0. Cover sequences enumerate countable covers with empty padding; the positive-diameter construction uses a subset of ℕ to avoid duplicating finite nonempty families. dimH is native, defined as the supremum of nonnegative exponents with infinite native unnormalized Hausdorff measure; its nonnegative extended codomain gives dimH empty=0. Positive real exponents are embedded by ENNReal.ofReal only with the relevant positivity; D remains dimH E in ℝ≥0∞ and its toReal value is used only downstream of T005's finiteness. Nat casts of n and constants are finite ENNReal values. Lebesgue measure/integrals in the slicing and interval workers are volume on ℝ and the nonnegative lintegral. All five M facts are supplied by direct pinned Mathlib use, not additional premises. Background notes remain optional node-local references. N outputs are unchanged; auxiliary T001 exposes the uniform metric-space normalization calculation already used in S001 so both Euclidean and real-interval instances can share it.", "inputs": [{"id": "T002", "binder": "h_T002", "type": "(∀ (k : ℕ) (A : Set (YuiEucl k)) (a : ℝ), 0 < a → YuiMeasure a A = MeasureTheory.Measure.hausdorffMeasure a A ∧ (dimH A < ENNReal.ofReal a → YuiMeasure a A = 0) ∧ (ENNReal.ofReal a < dimH A → YuiMeasure a A = ⊤) ∧ (YuiMeasure a A = 0 → dimH A ≤ ENNReal.ofReal a) ∧ (YuiMeasure a A = ⊤ → ENNReal.ofReal a ≤ dimH A)) ∧ (∀ (k : ℕ) (A : Set (YuiEucl k)), 0 ≤ dimH A) ∧ (∀ (k : ℕ) (A B : Set (YuiEucl k)), A ⊆ B → dimH A ≤ dimH B) ∧ (∀ (k l : ℕ) (A : Set (YuiEucl k)) (g : A → YuiEucl l), Isometry g → dimH (Set.range g) = dimH A)"}, {"id": "T005", "binder": "h_T005", "type": "(0 ≤ dimH E ∧ dimH E ≤ (n : ℝ≥0∞) ∧ dimH E < ⊤) ∧ (∀ (s δ : ℝ), 0 < s → 0 < δ → YuiContent s δ E < ⊤)"}, {"id": "T011", "binder": "h_T011", "type": "∀ s δ : ℝ, 0 < s → 0 < δ → YuiContent s δ E ≤ YuiContent (s + 1) δ (YuiCylinder E)"}], "target": "0 < dimH E → dimH E + 1 ≤ dimH (YuiCylinder E)", "explanation": "Complete N005. For every real 0<s<D, N001 gives H^s(E)=top. The scale contents are monotone as δ decreases, so their supremum being top means arbitrarily large small-scale values. T011 transfers them to F at exponent s+1; hence H^{s+1}(F)=top and N001 gives ofReal(s+1)≤dimH F. Under D>0 and the finite D of N002 choose s=D.toReal*(1-1/j), j≥2, and pass the increasing real exponents to D. All displayed assumptions stay in the implication.", "source_steps": [{"id": "S022", "text": "Introduce L1: D>0 and, for arbitrary s>0, L2: s<D. N002 gives finite D and N001 gives H^s(E)=infinity. From the definition H^s(E)=sup_{delta>0}H^s_delta(E) and the fact that decreasing the scale only restricts admissible covers, H^s_delta(E) is unbounded as delta decreases to zero: given a finite level, choose a scale exceeding that level in content; every smaller positive scale does as well."}, {"id": "S023", "text": "N004 gives H^s_delta(E)≤H^{s+1}_delta(F) at every delta>0. By F001 the right side is unbounded at small scales. Therefore its supremum H^{s+1}(F)=infinity. Since s+1>0, N001 gives dimH(F)≥s+1."}, {"id": "S024", "text": "Discharge L2 and quantify s: dimH(F)≥s+1 for every 0<s<D. With finite positive D from N002 and L1, take s=D(1-1/j) for positive integers j≥2. These lie in (0,D) and increase to D, so the order inequalities give dimH(F)≥D+1. Discharge L1 to obtain the full implication in the exported claim."}], "boundary": "Only listed inputs are project premises. The pinned Mathlib environment is freely available; no sibling proof is supplied.", "background_supplement_sha256": "1bf0b9c7347572e230e12960e1ad72681eb160b097abdd7fb42c849256a378a3", "objects": [], "representations": [], "bridges": [], "shared_inputs": [], "background_note_index": [{"id": "R005.BG001", "at": "/inference/argument/1/text", "kind": "mathematical", "fact": "For families x_delta,y_delta in [0,infinity] indexed by delta>0, if sup_delta x_delta=infinity and x_delta≤y_delta for every delta, then sup_delta y_delta=infinity. If x_eta≥x_delta whenever 0<eta≤delta, then for every finite M there is delta_0>0 such that x_eta>M for all 0<eta≤delta_0."}, {"id": "R005.BG002", "at": "/inference/argument/2/text", "kind": "mathematical", "fact": "For a finite real d>0 and X∈[0,infinity], if X≥s+1 for every real 0<s<d, then the sequence s_j=d(1−1/j), integers j≥2, has 0<s_j<d and s_j↑d, and its bounds imply X≥d+1."}]}}
